# `project.json` here is a fixture — the body the read API serves for one
# project — and Nx's built-in project discovery claims every `project.json` it
# can see, which made this one an empty project named "contract" that owned
# this directory and ran nothing.
#
# Ignored *here* rather than in the root `.nxignore` on purpose. Nx reads the
# root file for change detection as well as for discovery, so a root entry would
# make an edit to this fixture affect nothing at all. Nx's change detection reads
# only the root file; its file walker honours this one too, so this hides the
# file from discovery and from the walker's hashes while a change to it still
# reaches every project whose inputs name it. The hash the walker no longer
# takes is taken by the `servedGoldens` named input's runtime entry in
# `nx.json`, so a cached reader still re-runs when this fixture moves.
# `tests/e2e/nx_affected.rs` holds both halves.
project.json
